| Feature                             |           Use for CL7? | Notes                                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| ----------------------------------- | ---------------------: | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Dynamic Data Masking**            |       Yes, but limited | Masks query results for non-privileged users, but real data remains in the table. Microsoft states DDM hides data in query results while the database value is not changed. ([Microsoft Learn][1])                             |
| **TDE**                             | Yes, baseline security | Encrypts database, backups, and logs at rest, but it does not mask data when queried. ([Microsoft Learn][2])                                                                                                                   |
| **Always Encrypted**                |                  Maybe | Stronger column-level encryption, but usually needs application/driver changes and can affect ETL/query logic. Microsoft documents separate setup, migration, and application development steps for it. ([Microsoft Learn][3]) |
| **Data Discovery & Classification** |                    Yes | Helps identify/classify PII but does not obfuscate the data by itself. ([Microsoft Learn][4])                                                                                                                                  |
| **Custom SQL/ETL obfuscation**      |          Best fallback | Permanently replaces PII in lower environments.                                                                                                                                                                                |

